<div class="card">
<h1>Portal Manual</h1>
<p><b>snltruckingusa.com</b> — your loads, your pay, your documents, your truck. One place.</p>
<p>This manual follows the menus exactly as you see them: <b>Home · Loads · Pay · My File · My Truck · More.</b></p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h2>0. Getting in</h2>
<ol><li>Go to <b>snltruckingusa.com</b> and tap <b>Staff Login</b>.</li><li>Log in with the username and temporary password the office sent you privately.</li><li>On your first login the site makes you set <b>your own password</b> (8 characters or more). Pick one you will remember — nobody at the company knows it after you change it.</li><li>After that, log in with your own password. Use <b>Password</b> (top of the screen) any time you want to change it, and <b>Logout</b> when you are done on a shared device.</li><li><b>Locked out or forgot your password?</b> Message the office. Your password gets reset to the temporary one and you set a new one at the next login. Don't wait days — message the same day.</li></ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h2>1. Home</h2>
<p>Your home screen is your day at a glance. Check it when you start your day:</p>
<ul><li><b>Today's loads</b> — the jobs on your plate today.</li><li><b>This week / last week pay snapshot</b> — a quick look, not the official statement (the official one is under <b>Pay</b>).</li><li><b>Documents expiring</b> — anything of yours expiring within 60 days shows here. Renew early; an expired medical card or license means you cannot legally drive.</li><li><b>Missing documents</b> — if a document is missing from your file, it is listed here. It shows on the office side too — expect a call.</li><li><b>Missing evidence</b> — recent loads that are still missing a ticket or proof. Clear these first; a load cannot be settled until its evidence is complete.</li><li><b>Safety Training progress</b> — how many topics you have acknowledged (see §7).</li></ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h2>2. Loads</h2>
<p><b>One trip = Order → Load out → Delivery → Empty return.</b> A trip is not finished when you deliver — it closes when the <b>empty-in ticket</b> lands. The customer pays the company only after the empty return is confirmed, and your settlement is calculated <b>from your tickets</b>. No ticket — no settlement for that part.</p>
<h3>Adding a load</h3>
<ol><li>Go to <b>Loads → My Loads</b> and use <b>Add from dispatch capture or ticket photo</b>.</li><li>Upload the dispatcher's order capture. The system reads the empty container and PIN, the load container, PIN and BOL, the delivery city and the appointment, and fills the form for you.</li><li><b>Read values are suggestions only — always check and fix them before saving.</b> A wrong container number or weight becomes your problem later; catching it now takes ten seconds.</li><li>Save. The load appears with <b>Step 1 — Dispatch: Waiting for owner approval</b>. The office approves the dispatch; you keep working — the next steps open as the job moves.</li></ol>
<h3>The ticket steps (they depend on the job type)</h3>
<ul><li><b>Standard job:</b> Load-in ticket → Load-out ticket → delivery → <b>Empty-in ticket (closes the job)</b>.</li><li><b>Load-in / empty-out job:</b> Load-in ticket → Empty-out ticket.</li><li><b>Empty-first job:</b> Empty return ticket → Load-out ticket → <b>Empty-in ticket (closes the job)</b>.</li></ul>
<p>Rules for every ticket photo: one ticket per photo, flat and straight, all four corners visible, no glare. The container number and weights are read from the load-out ticket automatically — check them against the paper ticket before you confirm.</p>
<h3>Ticket mismatch warning</h3>
<p>If the container numbers on your tickets do not match each other, the load shows a <b>⚠ Ticket mismatch</b> flag. Fix it the same day: re-upload the correct ticket, or correct the entry. A mismatched load cannot be confirmed.</p>
<h3>Pre-pull (helping another driver)</h3>
<p>Returned another driver's empty (<b>+$60</b>) or pulled another driver's load out (<b>+$75</b>)?</p>
<ol><li>Submit it in the pre-pull section on the Loads page <b>with the terminal ticket photo</b> — no ticket, no credit.</li><li>The office approves it, and the matching amount is deducted from the other driver's side. It joins your week income once approved.</li></ol>
<h3>Detention</h3>
<ul><li>The first <b>2 hours</b> of waiting are included. After that, detention pays <b>$50/hour</b>.</li><li>Enter the detention on the load <b>and</b> send the office the dispatcher's message about the wait. <b>The dispatcher's message is the only evidence accepted</b> — no message, no detention pay. The time on your POD alone is not enough.</li></ul>
<h3>Pending vs Confirmed</h3>
<ul><li><b>Pending</b> = the office has not confirmed it yet. Check that your tickets are all in — that is usually what it is waiting on.</li><li><b>Confirmed</b> = locked into your settlement for that week.</li></ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h2>3. Fuel</h2>
<p><b>Loads → Fuel.</b> Enter every fueling <b>the same day</b>:</p>
<ul><li>Date, gallons, the pump price and the TCS price, and your odometer.</li><li>Fuel is settled at the <b>TCS discounted price</b> — that is the number your settlement uses.</li><li>Keep your receipts.</li><li>Your entries build your <b>weekly MPG</b> (shown on your statement). The company standard is <b>6.0 MPG</b> — below that, your statement flags it. Your gallons are a mirror, not a punishment: the numbers show your real driving, and because pay is split, excess fuel comes out of both sides.</li></ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h2>4. Pay (Settlement)</h2>
<p><b>Pay → Settlement.</b> This is your official weekly statement.</p>
<ul><li>The pay week runs <b>Sunday to Saturday</b>.</li><li>Settlements are paid <b>every Friday, one week in arrears</b>.</li><li>Check your statement <b>every week</b>, before Friday. After the week closes, corrections are slower.</li></ul>
<h3>How to read your statement</h3>
<p>For each load: the rate, plus any extras — <b>overweight</b> (judged on the cargo weight: 20ft over 39,000 lb / 40ft over 45,000 lb / reefer 40ft over 44,000 lb), <b>fuel surcharge</b>, <b>reefer</b> ($75 = $37.50 to set up + $37.50 to remove), <b>detention</b>, and <b>pre-pull</b> credits. Then:</p>
<p><b>Your pay = your split % of (total income − fuel − insurance).</b> Insurance is $100 per load day.</p>
<h3>Your split</h3>
<ul><li>First 3 months: <b>45%</b> → then <b>50%</b> → after 1 year: <b>55%</b>.</li><li><b>Weekend rule:</b> Saturday/Sunday work pays <b>70%</b> when you worked the full week (Mon–Fri) of that week <b>and</b> the following week, with no absence. The system judges it from your records; the owner confirms it at settlement.</li><li>The full rate table is under <b>More → Rates &amp; Pay</b>.</li></ul>
<h3>If a number looks wrong</h3>
<ol><li>Open the load and check the tickets and amounts first — most questions answer themselves there.</li><li>Still wrong? <b>Message the office with the date and the container number.</b> One clear message beats three phone calls.</li><li>A confirmed statement <b>can</b> be corrected when there is a real mistake. The correction reopens the statement, the change is recorded in the history — <b>nothing is ever changed quietly</b>, on either side.</li><li>Asking a question is never a problem. Waiting and guessing is.</li></ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h2>5. My File</h2>
<p><b>My File</b> is your driver qualification file — the file a federal auditor asks for. It has two parts:</p>
<h3>Your profile</h3>
<p>Your name, address, phone and emergency contact. If you edit your profile, the change goes to the office as <b>pending</b> and becomes official when the owner approves it. Keep it current — if your phone number changes, this is where it changes.</p>
<h3>Your documents</h3>
<p>Upload each document under its own item, and <b>enter the expiry date</b> where the item asks for one. A clear photo or a PDF (see the photo rules in §2). Your side of the list:</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<tr><th>Document</th><th>Expiry date?</th></tr>
<tr><td>CDL (license copy)</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><td>DOT Medical Card</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><td>TWIC Card</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
<tr><td>Driver Application</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>Signed Contract (+ Amendment)</td><td>No</td></tr>
<tr><td>W-9</td><td>No</td></tr>
</table></div>
<p>The blank forms are on each item — <b>download the form, fill it out, sign it, and upload the completed copy.</b></p>
<p>Four items are marked <b>Company</b> — MVR, Clearinghouse Query Result, Drug Test Result, Road Test Record. The office keeps those; you cannot upload them, and you do not need to ask about them. If one of them is missing, it is the office's job, not yours.</p>
<p><b>Pending vs confirmed:</b> your upload shows as pending until the owner reviews it. The current confirmed copy stays in place until the new one is confirmed — you are never left without a valid copy on file.</p>
<p><b>Renewals:</b> when you renew a license, medical card or TWIC, upload the new one right away — don't wait to be asked.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h2>6. My Truck</h2>
<p><b>My Truck</b> is your truck's file.</p>
<ul><li><b>Truck details</b> — your truck number, full VIN and plate. Check they match your truck; tell the office if anything is off.</li><li><b>Vehicle documents</b> — upload under each item, with the expiry date:</li></ul>
<p>  - <b>Registration / Cab Card</b> (yours to upload)</p>
<p>  - <b>Annual Inspection</b> (yours to upload)</p>
<p>  - Insurance Certificate, Title/Lease and any Overweight Permit are <b>Company</b> items — the office keeps them.</p>
<p>  - Same rule as your own file: a new upload is pending until confirmed, and the <b>confirmed copy is the official one</b> — that is the copy you show at roadside.</p>
<ul><li><b>Repairs</b> — report a defect or a repair here as soon as you notice it. Do your <b>DVIR in the ELD app before driving</b> and report defects right away — the portal record and the ELD record must tell the same story.</li></ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h2>7. Safety Training</h2>
<p><b>Home → Safety Training</b> (also under <b>More</b>). Short topics — a few minutes each:</p>
<p>Vehicle inspection · Container &amp; chassis safety · Speed, distance &amp; braking · Backing &amp; blind spots · Fatigue &amp; hours of service · No phone while rolling · Seat belts · Weather, night &amp; deer · Port &amp; terminal safety · If an accident happens · Cargo, seals &amp; placards · The professional mindset.</p>
<p>Read the topic and tap <b>Acknowledge</b>. Your acknowledgment is recorded with the date — this is part of your safety file. When a new topic appears, do it that week.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h2>8. More</h2>
<ul><li><b>Company Rules</b> — the full rules and the Driver Start Kit (what every driver brings: your documents, your toolbox in the side box, cab gear — and what never goes in the truck).</li><li><b>Rates &amp; Pay</b> — the rate table and the pay rules in full.</li><li><b>Benefits</b> — vacation (14 days, 7 paid), the $700 birthday payment if your vacation is unused, and the $1,000 Thanksgiving bonus, as they apply to you.</li></ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h2>9. The rules that matter most</h2>
<ul><li><b>No driving over 70 mph.</b> Warning first; repeated violations can end the contract.</li><li><b>Never edit your ELD records.</b> Log editing is prohibited — for everyone, no exceptions.</li><li><b>Never bobtail for personal use — no exceptions.</b> The company carries no bobtail insurance. The tractor moves only with a trailer, on company business.</li><li><b>Pick up and return your own containers</b> (no pre-pull) — unless the office assigns a pre-pull, which is paid as in §2.</li><li><b>Phone mounted and hands-free on every trip.</b> No phone while rolling.</li><li><b>No ticket — no settlement for that part.</b> Upload every ticket the same day.</li><li>Consequences: 1st violation — written warning. 2nd — settlement hold and a meeting. Serious violations (drunk driving, ELD tampering, leaving without notice) — immediate termination.</li></ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h2>10. If something is wrong</h2>
<ul><li><b>Pay or load question</b> → message the office with the <b>date + container number</b> (§4).</li><li><b>Login problem</b> → message the office the same day (§0).</li><li><b>A date, amount or document looks wrong</b> → say so right away. Every correction is recorded in the open — yours and ours.</li><li><b>An accident</b> → safety first, then call the office immediately, and save your dashcam footage. The full steps are in the Safety Training topic "If an accident happens."</li></ul>
<p><i>This system only works if we all use it the same way. Thank you.</i></p>
</div>
